# Pinned commit SHAs for the sibling-path replace targets in go.mod
# (../sh, ../bashsharp, ../coreutils, ../yoke, ../readline, ../filebrowser).
# scripts/bootstrap-siblings.sh reads this file and
# clones each sibling at the listed SHA, so standalone clones of bashy (and
# CI) build without external setup. coreutils and yoke themselves replace
# ../sh (and yoke replaces ../coreutils), which resolve to the same flat
# siblings.
#
# Inside the dhnt umbrella the siblings already exist as submodules
# (dhnt/sh, dhnt/bashsharp, dhnt/coreutils, dhnt/yoke) — the bootstrap script detects them and leaves
# them alone, so there is still exactly one copy of each.
#
# Format: <name>=<sha>. When bumping a sibling in the umbrella's
# script/sync.sh, the SHA here is bumped to match — sync.sh automates this.
#
# These SHAs are the ONLY sibling source CI ever sees. A local build cannot
# catch a stale pin: the umbrella mounts the live siblings as submodules, so
# the pins are never consulted here. scripts/hooks/pre-push therefore refuses
# a push while a pin disagrees with its sibling's HEAD; run
# scripts/update-sibling-pins.sh to resync.
sh=474334401b4635272fee097ed6257a5ca33397f0
bashsharp=34071a3ed4eca487518dbe5737fa6f61c86eb354
coreutils=abcde5b18ae23c8d50a8611a3f5da6e78c329cad
yoke=66bfd3e1495dae3f8fdee94a80f4f4f28a1ba642
readline=b958823bd7075ed8b9a3aedd351422356a95fe79
filebrowser=c350ca3e5ad072f1db9e4c8a1b143184d7a58f8a
